---
alwaysApply: true
---
Everything is driven by github issues and PRs.
Before writing any code, come up with a clear design on what has to happen in the issue body. Consider this as documentation of the PR. 
Once the feature is ready to be implemented, create a new branch and open a pull request. 
In each pull request, ensure the documentation in the docs/* has been updated to reflect the changes. 
The issue body is the PR description.